{
  "_comment": "Bosses. Each lairs at a fixed point in its system and appears while players are there (respawnSeconds after it dies; its system left empty is remembered as it is, a living boss mending slowly: rules.json memory). hp scales every part; damage scales its guns; speed is its engine output (up to 2.5, above any player design: how fast it flies and turns). Phases trigger as its hull integrity falls below `at`: say (announced to the system), escorts (ships that join it), enrage (damage multiplier from then on), heal (fraction of every part restored), blink (teleports next to its target every N ticks), nova (a telegraphed ring of shots every N ticks: kind, count, warnTicks). Everyone who damaged it (or was close when it died) gets XP, credits and their own loot roll, straight into storage.",
  "rules": {
    "creditRange": 5000,
    "creditWindowTicks": 3600,
    "barRange": 7000,
    "repeatCredits": 0.25,
    "_stageCover": "Staged bosses: a hit on a later stage's part (under the plates) passes to the nearest current-stage plate at this share. A boss's own stageCover overrides it.",
    "stageCover": 0.4
  },
